# FITS data (large binary files)
FITSDATA/
datafiles/
*.fit
*.fits

# compiled Python
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo

# macOS metadata
.DS_Store

# IDE / editor config
.idea/
.vscode/
.claude/
.cursor/

# generated outputs and local data — our actual data/renders, never shipped to git
tmpimg/
final-imgs/
generated/
paperfigs/

# local dev / project management
# Markdown is ignored by default (agent scratch, handoffs, working notes), then
# re-admitted BY LOCATION, not by extension:
#
#   docs/     operator- and science-facing documents. Tracked. Anything a fresh
#             clone of the observatory PC needs to run a night goes here — the
#             PC gets code by `git pull`, and a procedure that only exists on
#             the developer's laptop is a procedure the operator does not have.
#   root      agent and session scratch. Stays ignored.
#
# Per-file negations below are grandfathered co-located docs that belong beside
# their code; do not add new ones — put new documents in docs/.
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
handoff*.md
*.md
!README.md
!next-session-prompts.md
!/docs/
!/docs/**
# Licensing files must never be silently dropped by the *.md rule. THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md
# is created at the root by RELICENSE-AGPLv3.md Step 2 and would otherwise be skipped by
# that step's `git add -A`, shipping the AGPL baseline with no third-party attribution.
!THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md
!/alpyca_tools/windows_bridge/checklist.md
!/qhy_alpaca/UPSTREAM.md
!/.codex/skills/*/SKILL.md
prompts/
reference-sheets/
reports/
tests/
!/tests/
!/tests/*.py

# PDFs (reference materials)
*.pdf
